<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia produces 1.41 mln bpd crude in July.</title>
<headline>Indonesia produces 1.41 mln bpd crude in July.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia produced 1.41 million barrels  per day of crude oil and around 165,000 bpd of condensate in July,  oil industry source said on Friday.</p>
<p>The 1.41 million barrels &quot;included around 60,000 bpd for own-use at  the Duri field&quot;, the source said.</p>
<p>Duri, operated by PT Caltex Pacific Indonesia, currently produces  around 290,000 bpd, but some 60,000 bpd was used for a steamflood  project.</p>
<p>Caltex is jointly owned by Chevron Corp AND Texaco Inc. The source  give no other details.</p>
<p>Indonesia has an OPEC quota of 1.33 million bpd.</p>
<p>--Jakarta newsroom +6221 3846364+</p>
</text>
